      'director.decision': lines([
      `- A stored goal does not require action every turn. ACT, NEUTRAL, NO_TARGET, SCENE_TRANSITION, and CONTINUE_LATER are all valid.`,
      `- A post-commit conditional plan can be discarded when the next user input establishes solitude, recollection, dreaming, departure, or a scene transition. Never depend on a remembered-only character physically appearing.`,
      `- In proof mode, choose an ACT when a fitting actor and target are forecast present. Otherwise use the correct non-action decision.`,
      `- Do not write the final roleplay response. Return only structured state updates and a goal/action plan.`,
      // 일반 행동 보수성 완화(2026-10-22, 계획서 8절): 제안이 기본, 중립은 구조적 이유에만, 점수·강도의 뜻, 저장 목표는 다음 칸으로.
      `- Propose by default. When an actor and a target are forecast present and the scene gives any opening, return ACT with the fitting move. NEUTRAL, NO_TARGET, SCENE_TRANSITION and CONTINUE_LATER are for structural reasons only (no cast, a transition, solitude, a political or mission scene without a relational opening, a stored goal that must wait for a condition), never because the move seems modest, early or unnecessary: how often proposals run is decided by the application and its settings, not by you.`,
      `- score is how well the move fits this character in this scene, not how cautious it is: 70 or more when the actor's values and the opening clearly support it, 40-69 when plausible, under 40 only when forced. intensity is how far the move goes this turn: 0 a hint, 50 an open move, 100 the full move.`,
      `- A stored goal advances: each ACT for it takes the next concrete step (nextMove), never a restatement of the previous one; when the target responded in kind (reciprocated true), the next step goes further.`,
      // 기록의 연속성(2026-10-29, Erosync.Pair-Contact.Work-Plan.md): pairContact(마지막 실제 접촉 한 줄)를 읽는 규칙. 모든 수위.
      `- pairContact gives, for each pair with a stored goal or target, the last move that actually ran between them (who made it, how many turns ago, what it was) and how many of the actor's moves toward this target ran in full, in part or not at all since the pair's first record. Continue from where the pair actually stands when the recent conversation does not show it; a long gap means they have not met since, not that the wish is gone, and whether it cooled follows the actor's goalPersistence and obsessiveness.`,
      ]),
      'director.language': lines([
      `- Language of this JSON result: write every descriptive text value in English, whatever language the conversation uses. This covers summaries, notes, reasons, descriptions, location, style, objective, currentApproach, nextMove, behaviorSignals pattern and summary${sfw ? '' : ', and preferenceSignals label and reason'}. When a preference item or behavior pattern is the same as one already present in the input (preferenceContext, developmentPatterns, behaviorDevelopment patterns), repeat that label or pattern text exactly as it is given there, in whatever language it is stored, instead of rewording or translating it. Names are not translated: a newly discovered character's name and aliases are written as they appear in the conversation. Fields defined as exact quotes stay verbatim in the conversation's own wording. This rule is about the text of this JSON result only. Never put an instruction about the language of the roleplay response into style, objective, currentApproach, nextMove, or any other field.`,
      `- Return only the requested fields and no unrelated policy fields.`,
      `- Every confidence field, including provisional-profile retaliation, rivalry-patch, and behavior-signal confidence, must be a JSON integer from 0 to 100, never a 0-1 fraction.`,
      ]),
